# inc-kgzx: photograph where "Undeath to Death" actually kills, BEFORE the
# phase-2 rules change.
#
# THE CLAIM, as the plan states it. lib/pspells.irh, "Undeath to Death" (the
# live spell near line 5872):
#     aval: AR_BALL; lval: 3; qval: Q_TAR; pval: (LEVEL_1PER1)d8; tval: MA_UNDEAD
# The Desc says a 60-foot globe centred on the caster; the code (src/Magic.cpp,
# the `if (isBall)` block) explodes where the shot LANDS: MinGlyphs =
# 3*e.EMagic->lval = 9 squares, about a 2-square radius around the aimed
# target. Q_TAR (src/Magic.cpp:859) makes the player pick a target first. Each
# undead caught then rolls its own (caster level)d8 in the EV_MAGIC_HIT handler
# and dies if that beats its current HP; there is no save.
#
# THE PHASE-2 SIDE, for contrast (NOT implemented here): a 4-square-radius
# burst (AR_GLOBE, lval 4) at the aimed point; ONE pool of (caster level)d4 Hit
# Dice per cast, max 20d4, spent fewest HD first, ties by distance to the
# centre; leftover too small for the next creature is wasted; no undead of 9+
# HD is affected; Will save negates; spell resistance applies.
#
# THE SCENE. The caster (orc priest of Aiswin, character level 11 through Free
# Advancement, "Undeath to Death" learned through Learn Any Spell so it is
# innate and its caster level is ChallengeRating = 11) stands at (44,111) in
# the Entry Chamber. The corridor east is open to x+9; a wall sits at x+10.
# Five undead are summoned in that corridor with Wizard Monster Summoning, on
# distinct squares:
#
#   D  caster+1  (45,111)  a crawling claw, 1 HD -- RIGHT NEXT TO THE CASTER,
#                          6 squares from the aim point: outside BOTH areas.
#   B  caster+4  (48,111)  a crawling claw, 1 HD -- 3 squares from the aim
#                          point: outside TODAY'S ~2-square spread, inside the
#                          phase-2 4-square radius. Radius observable.
#   T  caster+7  (51,111)  a crawling claw, 1 HD -- THE AIMED TARGET.
#   K  caster+8  (52,111)  a bodak, 9 HD (lib/mon3.irh:3422) -- 1 square from
#                          the aim point: inside both areas. TODAY it dies
#                          whenever the d8 roll beats its HP; under phase 2 the
#                          9+ HD cap leaves it untouched. Cap observable.
#
# Freeze Monsters (armed in the shared setup) keeps all five on their squares
# while the screens are photographed; Wizard Sight makes the far end of the
# corridor perceivable so the target prompt accepts T and K.
#
# THE TARGET PROMPT. Q_TAR's cursor (src/Term.cpp:2595) is a ring of candidates
# ordered by bearing from the player; these creatures all lie due east, so the
# ring order is by distance. The first RIGHT enters on the nearest (D, +1),
# then RIGHT steps to B (+4), then to T (+7), then to K (+8). Three RIGHTs
# confirm on the aimed target T.
#
# Run:
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_RUN_DIR="$PWD/logs/inc-kgzx/before/seed-1" \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/undeath-to-death-area.keys 1
@include undeath-to-death-setup.keys

# --- SUMMON D, THE CLAW BESIDE THE CASTER (CASTER+1) ------------------------
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
TAB
@choose "Zombies"
@choose "crawling claw"
RIGHT
ENTER
@dump:summon-d

# --- SUMMON B, THE CLAW THREE SQUARES FROM THE AIM POINT (CASTER+4) ---------
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
TAB
@choose "Zombies"
@choose "crawling claw"
RIGHT*4
ENTER
@dump:summon-b

# --- SUMMON T, THE AIMED TARGET (CASTER+7) ----------------------------------
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
TAB
@choose "Zombies"
@choose "crawling claw"
RIGHT*7
ENTER
@dump:summon-t

# --- SUMMON K, THE 9-HD BODAK INSIDE THE AREA (CASTER+8) --------------------
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Outsiders"
@choose "bodak"
RIGHT*8
ENTER
@dump:summon-k

# --- CAST UNDEATH TO DEATH, AIMED AT T --------------------------------------
m
@choose "Undeath to Death"
RIGHT*3
@dump:target-prompt
ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:after-cast
v
@dump:messages
@while "Messages" ESC
@quit
